A||||4||Phil||Dodge Dakota Magnum V6||||5||
Z||000000||Phil||08-14-2000||10:21 PM||||Does anybody have any input on this engine/motor as to reliability, longevity and general all around goodness? Looking at a 97 4X4<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||AkursedX||08-14-2000||11:47 PM||||Well my brother owns a 97 4x4 Dakota with a v-6.  <BR>Well....when he first got it, he had to have a brand new engine put in.  I can't remember the exact problem, I think it was due to some excess metal in the engine that caused alot of problems.  But since he had the new engine put in, it has been fine.  I think there's about 48k miles on it now. <BR>As far as power, it's adequate.  I live in Buffalo NY, and got my car stuck in the snow one day and he towed me out of it. Plus it is much better on gas than the v-8's.  I don't know an exact amount though, but I think he gets somewhere between 20-25 mpg.<P>The only other major problem he had with the truck was cosmetic.  The black paint on the bumpers peeled off very quickly and it rusted real bad.  But he got that fixed under warranty.<P>Overall, they are pretty good trucks.  I mean you're not going to blow the doors off of anyone, but it is quick enough.  It does ride a little harsh and a little sluggish, but I drive a Fiero all the time, so of course it will feel like that to me. lol<BR>And for a truck, I'd recommend it.  Well that of course depends on the shape of it and the price, lol.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Hope I was of assitance.||||reg||4
Z||000002||Phoenix||08-15-2000||10:49 AM||||My x drives an 98 Dakota 4x2 with the v6. It's been a good truck and the only problem has been a plugged cat/Converter. Gets ok mpg and power is reasonable.  I just purchased a 2000 Dakota Quad Cab with the 4.7 v8. Big difference  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Performance is great and it still gets 18 - 19 mpg with "real" room for 4 people.  I have a cousin thats a transmission specialist for a Dodge dealer and I trust his  judgenment when he says that the Dakotas are good reliable trucks.||||reg||1
Z||000003||wahoo4u||08-15-2000||10:20 PM||||personal opinion here.  I have driven the dakota with the 5.2 in it.  Almost too much power for the truck.  I have also heard a few owners of the v6 complaining of lack of power.  gas milage was never complained about.  i have also heard of the v6 not lasting as long as the v8.  Personal preference, i would go for the 5.2 over the 3.9 even with the difference in gas milage.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fformula88||08-17-2000||04:56 PM||||My grandfather has a 2000 Dakota SLT club cab with the 3.9L V6.  I think its a very nice engine.  It has very good pickup from what I would expect in a pickup.  We have never raced, but I think its probably faster than my Fiero Formula by a little bit off the line.  At speed, it feels almost identical.  Its quick for a truck.  Gas milage has been low, but it doesn't have many miles on it so the engine is still green.<P>Overall, I am not highly impressed by the trucks build quality.  There are spots in the paint around corners where its not too smooth.  Some buffing could fix it, but I am not sure I want to attempt it because the clear coat could be thin there.  Also, the box was installed crooked and off center from the factory.  Even the rear axle wasn't straight.  This was causing the truck to pull to the right.  The dealer was able to loosen everything up and get it all straightened out.<P>Since April, we haven't had any mechanical problems besides the bed.  I do like the truck, but am not convinced it will hold up well.  It just seems cheaply assembled to me.  ||||reg||1
